==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Thor Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Maximum the Fighter''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Think of this Cat, especially in Normal and Evolved Form, as a heavier version of [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Axe Cat]] or [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Ninja Cat]], trading cost and cooldown for significantly higher health and attack power. Its rapid attack speed, Strong against Red ability, decent attack damage and VERY high health for its cost makes it an incredibly well-rounded Cat with no real weaknesses until [[Teacher Bun Bun|Bun Bun]]'s debut. Once you obtain this Cat in early game, Viking Cat will destroy the first 2 chapters of [[Empire of Cats]]. He is also considerably helpful for [[Festival Gross (Insane)|Crazed Gross]], [[Flappy Cat (Insane)|Crazed Bird]] and [[Crazy Cats (Insane)|Crazed Titan]].

However, as the game progresses, Viking Cat's stats fall off substantially as superior anti-Red specialists like [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]] become available.

==='''True Form'''===
Maximum the Fighter's high stats make it a very valuable asset in any anti-red army, especially in 4-crown [[Stories of Legend]]. Outside of 4-crown, he can be superfluous at times, mainly due to [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat's]] far higher defensive capabilities and competition from [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Normal]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic]] Island. As a meatshield he's also outclassed by [[Carpenter Cat (Rare Cat)|Carpenter Cat]] since Carpenter has higher bulk and doesn't get juggled frequently, alongside having more relevant immunities and an additional niche for Floating threats. The only advantage Maximum the Fighter has over Carpenter is higher effective health and DPS, though this rarely matters as Carpenter is generally better at holding the frontline while other attackers rain damage from afar.

==='''Talents'''===
The Weaken and Slow immunities are situational talents for Maximum, as they can both only come into play in a handful of stages and for not great effect, with the main exceptions being all of the stages that feature [[Hannya]] and some of the stages that feature [[Professor A.]], but not as a direct counter to the latter, rather to keep the pressure on enemy frontliners despite the slow. Resistance to Toxic and Curse are way too situational and barely effective to be worth any NP. This leaves the health buff as the only truly worthwhile upgrade, as Maximum is very effective in 4-crown [[Legend Stages|Stories of Legend]], where higher survivability would definitely help.

==='''Orb'''===
Despite having the Strong ability, Defense Up against Red is recommended, as it offers a bigger increase to the unit's survivability, while the extra damage provided by Strong Up is negligible at best.

